</p>
<p>54 minutes. Between the ant&#8217;s two encounters with the minute hand, the hand passed over 45 minute marks. In that time, the ant passed over 105 minute marks (45 minutes plus one complete circumference). The ratio of their speeds was thus 45/105, or 3/7. If <em>x</em> minutes elapsed before their first encounter, then in that time the minute hand advanced by <em>x</em> minutes while the ant crawled over 30 &#8211; <em>x</em> minute marks. So <em>x</em>/(30 &#8211; <em>x</em>) = 3/7, which gives <em>x</em> = 9 minutes, and the total time is 9 + 45 = 54 minutes.</p>
